      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 2.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0",
      "artist": "Humphrey Bolton",
      "description": "Victoria Theatre, Halifax. This is the Fountain Street side of the entrance part of the theatre. All round the theatre the names of composers, presumably of operas, are inscribed. The three in this view are Bishop, Wallace and Arne. \nHenry Rowley Bishop was born in London in 1786 and died there in 1855.  He was the first musician to be knighted. The famous song 'Home Sweet Home' is from one of his operas. \nWilliam Vincent Wallace was born in Waterford, Ireland, in 1812 and died in 1865. He wrote two very successful operas: 'Maritana' and 'Lurline'. \nSee 1404904 for William Wallace's memorial in Waterford.\n\nThomas Augustine Arne is the only one of the three who is still well-known.  He was born in London in 1710 and died there in 1778. 'Rule Britannia' comes from his masque 'Alfred'. He wasn't really an operatic composer; his opera 'Artaxerxes' has some success, but was old-fashioned at the time.",
      "dateCreated": "2009-03-20",
      "categories": [
        "CC-BY-SA-2.0",
        "Images by Humphrey Bolton",
        "Images from Geograph Britain and Ireland",
        "Information field template with formatting",
        "Taken with Panasonic Lumix DMC-TZ3",
        "United Kingdom photographs taken on 2009-03-20",
        "Victoria Theatre, Halifax"
      ],
      "sourceType": "commons-category",
      "sourceArticleId": "victoria-theatre-halifax-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "gcw9",
